.TH SDL_ConvertPixelsAndColorspace 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ConvertPixelsAndColorspace \- Copy a block of pixels of one format and colorspace to another format and colorspace.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_surface.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_ConvertPixelsAndColorspace(int width, int height, SDL_PixelFormat src_format, SDL_Colorspace src_colorspace, SDL_PropertiesID src_properties, const void *src, int src_pitch, SDL_PixelFormat dst_format, SDL_Colorspace dst_colorspace, SDL_PropertiesID dst_properties, void *dst, int dst_pitch);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I width
the width of the block to copy, in pixels\[char46]
.TP
.I height
the height of the block to copy, in pixels\[char46]
.TP
.I src_format
an
.BR SDL_PixelFormat
value of the
.BR src
pixels format\[char46]
.TP
.I src_colorspace
an
.BR SDL_Colorspace
value describing the colorspace of the
.BR src
pixels\[char46]
.TP
.I src_properties
an
.BR SDL_PropertiesID
with additional source color properties, or 0\[char46]
.TP
.I src
a pointer to the source pixels\[char46]
.TP
.I src_pitch
the pitch of the source pixels, in bytes\[char46]
.TP
.I dst_format
an
.BR SDL_PixelFormat
value of the
.BR dst
pixels format\[char46]
.TP
.I dst_colorspace
an
.BR SDL_Colorspace
value describing the colorspace of the
.BR dst
pixels\[char46]
.TP
.I dst_properties
an
.BR SDL_PropertiesID
with additional destination color properties, or 0\[char46]
.TP
.I dst
a pointer to be filled in with new pixel data\[char46]
.TP
.I dst_pitch
the pitch of the destination pixels, in bytes\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
The same destination pixels should not be used from two threads at once\[char46] It is safe to use the same source pixels from multiple threads\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_ConvertPixels (3)
